  "notes": "USAGE:\n{記載|きさい} is used in formal, written contexts — documents, forms, contracts, and official records. It is more formal than {書|か}く (to write) and implies recording information in an organized, official manner. The passive form {記載|きさい}されている (is listed/recorded) is particularly common when referring to information already written in a document.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {記載|きさい}する: to record, to list\n- {記載|きさい}{事項|じこう}: items to be recorded\n- {記載|きさい}{内容|ないよう}: recorded content\n- {記載|きさい}{漏|も}れ: omission in recording",
